    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.5 测试版\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n- 登录页按后台当前配置分别启用短信验证码、邮箱验证码和微信扫码登录；短信与邮箱会使用各自的标签、占位提示、格式校验、验证码长度及发送间隔。\n- 账号密码登录始终保留。验证码渠道全部关闭时自动切换到密码登录；微信扫码未开启时展示明确的不可用状态，不再请求二维码接口。\n- 密码登录不再携带邀请码，验证码登录继续支持邀请注册；修复 HTTP 环境、Clipboard API 不可用或浏览器拒绝授权时无法复制邀请链接的问题。\n- 用户端与管理端在未配置品牌素材时统一使用官方 AID Logo 与 Favicon，管理员配置的自定义品牌素材仍优先生效。\n- 支付宝与微信支付均关闭时隐藏用户端充值入口，任一支付渠道启用后自动恢复显示。\n- 修复首次安装或失败重试时对数据目录归属的误判：保留启动前目录快照，支持 Docker 与非 Docker 部署相互切换恢复，同时继续拦截未知文件、目录和软链接。\n- 加固升级器备份保留策略，仅清理升级器自身生成且符合命名规则的历史备份；用户目录、普通文件及软链接不会被纳入清理范围。\n- 完善 CentOS 7 等旧发行版上的 Redis 编译工具链兼容与下载校验，并更新三端 README 中的一键部署、配置、升级和卸载说明。\n- 新增可重复执行的 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.5.sql`，为旧数据库补齐短信、邮箱和微信登录开关，且不覆盖管理员已有配置；全新部署继续以 `sql/aid-init.sql` 为初始化真源。\n\n\u003e 本版本为 Beta 测试版。升级会从版本标签构建三端程序，CPU 与内存占用会在构建阶段明显升高。升级前请备份数据库和部署配置，并先在测试环境验证登录、支付入口、安装重试与在线升级流程。\n\n# AID v1.0.0-beta.5 Beta Release\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n- The login page now enables SMS code, email code, and WeChat QR login independently from the active server configuration. SMS and email use channel-specific labels, placeholders, validation, code length, and resend intervals.\n- Password login remains available at all times. When both verification-code channels are disabled, the page automatically selects password login; when WeChat login is disabled, the page shows an explicit unavailable state without requesting a QR code.\n- Password login no longer sends invitation codes, while verification-code registration continues to support invitations. Invitation-link copying now falls back safely when the Clipboard API is unavailable, blocked, or used over HTTP.\n- The Web and admin applications now fall back to the official AID logo and favicon when custom branding is not configured. Administrator-provided branding still takes precedence.\n- Recharge entry points are hidden when both Alipay and WeChat Pay are disabled and return automatically when either payment channel is enabled.\n- Fixed data-root ownership detection during first installation and failed-install retries. The installer snapshots the original directory state, supports recovery when switching between Docker and non-Docker deployment, and continues to reject unknown files, directories, and symbolic links.\n- Hardened updater backup retention so it prunes only updater-generated backup directories with valid managed names. User directories, regular files, and symbolic links are never included in pruning.\n- Improved Redis build-toolchain compatibility and download verification on CentOS 7 and other older distributions, and refreshed the deployment, configuration, upgrade, and uninstall guidance in all three READMEs.\n- Added the repeatable `sql/v1.0.0-beta.5.sql` migration to backfill SMS, email, and WeChat login switches without overwriting administrator values. Fresh installations continue to use `sql/aid-init.sql` as the single initialization source.\n\n\u003e This is a Beta release. Building the three applications from signed source tags can temporarily consume significant CPU and memory. Back up the database and deployment configuration, then validate login, payment visibility, failed-install recovery, and online upgrade flows in a staging environment before production use.",
